<article class="env-definition" id="09GC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09GC">Definition <span data-tag="09GC">9.8.1</span>.</a> Consider a field extension $F/E$. An element $\alpha \in F$ is said to be <em>algebraic</em> over $E$ if $\alpha $ is the root of some nonzero polynomial with coefficients in $E$. If all elements of $F$ are algebraic then $F$ is said to be an <em>algebraic extension</em> of $E$. </p>
</article>